= The <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> Enters Government

Staal has concluded that he needs broader popular and parliamentary support beyond the <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**DSU**</span>, and has opened talks with Aurelian Renck to secure the backing of the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>. Renck has proven far more willing to cooperate with Staal than he ever was with Goodryke, and the party itself is eager to return to government.

The main obstacle, however, is the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>’s deep reservations about sharing a cabinet with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>. To overcome this, Staal and the <span style="color: #6A1E1E;">**DSU**</span> have signaled their readiness to fast-track a <i>Reichskonkordat</i> with the Vatican—an offer that Renck, a longtime advocate of such, finds difficult to refuse.

- @z_in_gov

@z_in_gov
title: Staal has found a new puppet in Renck.
on-arrival: kaas_puppet = 1; unionist_in_gov = 1; unionist_relation -= 20; pro_republic -= 5; staal_approval += 1; dufour_staal_r += 1

The <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> claims its ministerial positions, with Adam Sedgewick securing the Labor Ministry, and other members taking the Transport and Justice portfolios. The <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> also brings the <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">**Arcanists**</span> into the fold, which is granted the Postal Ministry.

With Aurelian Renck’s connections in the southern courts, the negotiation of a <i>Reichskonkordat</i> is fast-tracked and set to be ready for signing in a few weeks.

However, their entry into government has strained our relations, as they had previously stood in united opposition with us.
